  "step_3": "The decision reason requires comparing variances and preferring the lower-variance lottery (B). However, the individual does not mention or appear to consider variance, spread, or risk in any form. Instead, the individual focuses solely on the small 5-percentage-point difference in the probability of winning and uses that as a justification to pick A. There is no evidence that the individual computed or considered second-order moments like variance. The information considered (win probability difference) is not the same as that required by the decision reason (variance). The justification (small difference in win chance) does not align with the rule of the decision reason (prefer lower variance). Therefore, it is unlikely that the individual used the variance-based decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 10
