  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on variance as a quantitative measure of risk and prefers the lottery with lower variance (Lottery A). However, the individual chose Lottery B and justified this by emphasizing the higher upside (6000 vs 3000) and accepting the higher risk for the chance of a larger gain. The individual did not consider or mention variance, nor any measure that correlates with it (e.g., spread, risk dispersion). Instead, the deliberation focused on best-case outcomes and their probabilities. There is no alignment between the information used by the reason (variance) and that considered by the individual (maximum gain, chance of high reward). Furthermore, the justification (seeking higher reward despite risk) contradicts the rationale of preferring lower variance. Therefore, it is certain that the individual did not use the variance-minimizing reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
}

